WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.280 --> 00:00:05.580
Electric cars and plug-in hybrids are all
the rage at the moment.

00:00:05.590 --> 00:00:10.410
But the Toyota Prius -- the grandfather of
them all -- has been out on the road for around

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:12.160
20 years now.

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:16.520
The Japanese carmaker has regularly updated
the technology of course.

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:20.840
The current model being sold in showrooms
is the vehicle's fourth generation.

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:29.320
Car tester Ines Petri explains that the latest
Prius comes in a full hybrid or plug-in version.

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:33.000
The latter is more for people who can run
a cable to the car at home.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:37.800
In the full hybrid, on the other hand, batteries
are charged by the gasoline engine out on

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:43.000
the road -- or by recovering energy during
braking and engine braking, she says.

00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:53.820
Ines is taking out the full-hybrid, self-charging
variant of the Prius.

00:00:53.829 --> 00:01:00.360
Its power is provided either by a 1-point-8-liter
gasoline engine and an electric motor that can also work

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:03.520
independently of its internal combustion counterpart.

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:08.270
A secondary electric motor converts power
from the gas engine into electrical energy

00:01:08.270 --> 00:01:10.020
stored in the batteries.

00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:14.140
Altogether, the system puts out 90 kilowatts
of power.

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:19.710
The Prius can hit 100 kilometers an hour from
a standstill in 10-point-6 seconds and has

00:01:19.710 --> 00:01:22.090
a top speed of 180.

00:01:22.090 --> 00:01:26.920
Toyota says it burns just 3-point-3 liters
of fuel per hundred kilometers.

00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:34.000
Ines says that over the years, Toyota has
managed to make the hybrid feel more and more

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:37.100
like a standard internal combustion engine
car.

00:01:39.080 --> 00:01:45.320
Drivers can choose different driving modes...
among them the environmentally friendly Eco-Mode,

00:01:45.320 --> 00:01:53.140
a Normal mode and a Power mode for when you
want a little more juice.

00:01:53.140 --> 00:01:55.660
The latter really gives the car a lot of zip.

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:03.890
There's also a purely electric mode for when
the car is travelling at low speeds.

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:08.960
However, the full hybrid only manages that
trick for around two kilometers.

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:14.260
And that's the decisive difference between
it and the plug-in version.

00:02:14.269 --> 00:02:20.189
The plug-in has larger batteries that give
it a range of about 50 kilometers.

00:02:20.189 --> 00:02:23.219
This variant is also 11 centimeters longer.

00:02:23.219 --> 00:02:28.870
But because the technology takes up more space,
Prius plug-ins have 140 liters less volume

00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:30.100
in the trunk.

00:02:32.170 --> 00:02:38.640
A two-part hatch has also been a character
trait in the model for the last two generations.

00:02:38.659 --> 00:02:43.489
The interior is a study in contrasts and anything
but boring.

00:02:43.489 --> 00:02:46.730
The dashboard display is narrow and sleek.

00:02:46.730 --> 00:02:50.640
A lot of the important data appears on a high-tech
central console.

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:58.500
The shifter also has a futuristic look and
feel.

00:03:10.760 --> 00:03:15.380
All these polished surfaces contribute to
the car's modern look, says Ines.

00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:18.800
But they can also start to look dusty pretty
quickly.

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:23.060
That's why she would recommend always carrying
a featherduster on board.

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:26.600
Just a swipe and everything gleams again.

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:30.540
The displays also make a very modern impression.

00:03:30.549 --> 00:03:35.729
Especially the one up here on the dashboard,
which lets you know what's going on in the

00:03:35.729 --> 00:03:36.880
car all the time.

00:03:38.920 --> 00:03:43.960
Another modern touch -- an induction plate
for charging your smartphone without having

00:03:43.969 --> 00:03:45.449
to plug it in.

00:03:45.449 --> 00:03:48.960
The most antiquated feature is the parking
brake in the footwell.

00:03:51.520 --> 00:03:56.340
Ines says electric and plug-in hybrid cars
are really taking off.

00:03:56.349 --> 00:04:01.389
But for her, a full hybrid vehicle like this
one still has a place, even though its range

00:04:01.389 --> 00:04:03.820
is much more restricted than a plug-in.

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:10.040
That's because not everyone has access to
charging cables at home...or just doesn't

00:04:10.040 --> 00:04:12.299
want to bother with cables all the time.

00:04:12.299 --> 00:04:17.660
In general, she thinks, a key moment for the
sector will come when the batteries can be

00:04:17.660 --> 00:04:23.960
charged through induction -- and you can dispense
with cables altogether.

